    "OtherAbstract": {
      "Type": "PIP",
      "Language": "eng",
      "AbstractText": "5 to 8% of women on oral contraception (OC) suffer from headaches or migraines. There is, for the moment, no serious pathogenic explanation of this phenomenon. Blood pressure and eyesight problems should be checked. Headache can at times be the sign of serious cerebro-vascular accidents; in such cases OC should be stopped immediately."
    }
